and New Zealand said they would investigate his links to the countries.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Euro plummets against US dollar: has the next financial crisis begun?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8cbd11cc237c1121bb968566f91b0e3162191b2b4090e2f0fd9b6c5c9473bc7a</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:15:22Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T14:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/euro-plummets-against-us-dollar-has-the-next-financial-crisis-begun/a-79549031--86ee12acb8f2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/euro-plummets-against-us-dollar-has-the-next-financial-crisis-begun/a-79549031?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The euro has fallen to a 17-month low against the dollar. That will make inflation worse in the EU, where political worries and concern over French debt are already troubling investors. Is a fiscal crisis at hand?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Military aircraft with 32 people on board crashes in southern Nigeria</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:07b4de91f233cc4bdb9030019085af6454191741f73cd5d7d7d061d898f0adbe</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:15:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T14:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/military-aircraft-with-32-people-on-board-crashes-in-southern-nigeria/a-79552403--6ad5344ba083.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/military-aircraft-with-32-people-on-board-crashes-in-southern-nigeria/a-79552403?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Rescue teams searched the crash site after the military aircraft went down in southern Nigeria. All 32 people on the plane are confirmed to have died.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Iran poised to exploit security vacuum as US leaves Iraq</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e3c3d7b51b3cad78402c0d22d8db38e0ff4e54b3358f523e8f2d23b3794ed389</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:15:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T14:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-poised-to-exploit-security-vacuum-as-us-leaves-iraq/a-79550833--9d1cbb2d4ce5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-poised-to-exploit-security-vacuum-as-us-leaves-iraq/a-79550833?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The end of the US military mission in Iraq leaves the Kurdistan region facing a severe security vacuum. As Erbil grapples with deep internal divisions, Tehran is well positioned to make strategic gains.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Trust in the German Constitutional Court is eroding — how can this be stopped?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e1953aa5a158114ce031ea7644af2ddcd54085c4ac36fc5a26559d0a7546ab1c</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:15:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T14:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trust-in-the-german-constitutional-court-is-eroding-how-can-this-be-stopped/a-79549211--cc048545c82f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trust-in-the-german-constitutional-court-is-eroding-how-can-this-be-stopped/a-79549211?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's top court, which turned 75 this year, is losing the population's trust, surveys show. Some say reforms in the way it picks candidates would help, to also accept candidates nominated by the far-right AfD.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>What China's new military foothold in Laos means for Southeast Asia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cbefa2eb45c3bf8dd31dcd5aec0214fd8727639b00e83447bf6df49d94447cd2</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:15:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T14:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-china-s-new-military-foothold-in-laos-means-for-southeast-asia/a-79548259--642cd34d5dd0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-china-s-new-military-foothold-in-laos-means-for-southeast-asia/a-79548259?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Beijing says its new Laos facility will train pilots. Analysts see a broader signal: China's growing military presence in mainland Southeast Asia.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Spy chief warns Russia conflict risk growing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f7d371337b55edb51146c147c65a82e30616abba5df5b7a5b4a0fa1318a29806</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:15:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T12:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-spy-chief-warns-russia-conflict-risk-growing/live-79542789--3bde17a9e96c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-spy-chief-warns-russia-conflict-risk-growing/live-79542789?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Moscow is already waging a "shadow war" against Europe, the head of Germany's foreign intelligence service says. The Left Party is taking a case over remarks by the CDU's Katherina Reiche to a top court. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Suspected pneumonic plague in Siberia: What we know about the disease</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6717c51eed4063d33da727ef41cc507b39465bac70566b1d94dd92b67e6f06fc</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:15:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T11:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/suspected-pneumonic-plague-in-siberia-what-we-know-about-the-disease/a-79547919--6c7e74a1d6ab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/suspected-pneumonic-plague-in-siberia-what-we-know-about-the-disease/a-79547919?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A worker at a plague research institute in Siberia has died, and nearly 200 of her contacts are under medical observation. Russian authorities deny a link to the bacterial infection. The US is monitoring the situation.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>German soccer: Can new coach Klopp turn things around?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:17dca57fda324a2d6da764ab07cb78cecd3f996f4468e7418665a74daf04fd4f</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:15:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T10:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-soccer-can-new-coach-klopp-turn-things-around/a-79547308--04a0262a4a50.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-soccer-can-new-coach-klopp-turn-things-around/a-79547308?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Jürgen Klopp has done things a little differently since becoming Germany coach. Casting a wider net for talent and trying to connect with players and country haven't made an immediate impact, but he is not bowed.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Bosnia election: New steps to prevent electoral fraud, but nationalist parties remain on top</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0f5a5df80e06a0455860ea481abd60861bdbc40f66a32257cad4787d5f854170</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:15:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T10:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bosnia-election-new-steps-to-prevent-electoral-fraud-but-nationalist-parties-remain-on-top/a-79544717--5102b97990e3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bosnia-election-new-steps-to-prevent-electoral-fraud-but-nationalist-parties-remain-on-top/a-79544717?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">New technology has stopped votes being cast on behalf of dead or absent voters, and turnout has fallen to a record low. But it was a case of deja vu in Bosnia's elections with the same parties winning.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>As rising seas threaten low-lying Pacific Islands, regional leaders call on the world to take climate more seriously</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:890edafe87d8f690a3e4d3b29c958b49e0884aaddae9d52038f64d5c5dc4a645</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:15:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T09:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/as-rising-seas-threaten-low-lying-pacific-islands-regional-leaders-call-on-the-world-to-take-climate/a-79540127--eb759682e424.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/as-rising-seas-threaten-low-lying-pacific-islands-regional-leaders-call-on-the-world-to-take-climate-more-seriously/a-79540127?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">For Pacific island nations, climate change is no distant threat. As seas rise, they're bringing the real-time consequences of a warming planet directly to world leaders in Tuvalu.</summary><category term="Climate" /></entry><entry><title>German and US scientists win Nobel Prize in medicine for research on brain activity</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fa0ffb19801b0735412a9cdcfa564ff53562ed896b8861226815abf31ccb41e2</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:15:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T09:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-and-us-scientists-win-nobel-prize-in-medicine-for-research-on-brain-activity/a-79544130--321b53505aba.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-and-us-scientists-win-nobel-prize-in-medicine-for-research-on-brain-activity/a-79544130?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Karl Deisseroth, Peter Hegemann and Georg Nagel won the award for discoveries that provide new insights into how we might treat blindness, depression, addiction and dementia.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Israel's mental health crisis in the wake of Oct. 7 attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2ab43b22ed4e1bf1997d37e01605ff07c9b2dd0489660d6b89181cd6102c7247</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:15:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T08:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/israel-s-mental-health-crisis-in-the-wake-of-oct-7-attacks/a-79507122--40bc5ac1f942.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/israel-s-mental-health-crisis-in-the-wake-of-oct-7-attacks/a-79507122?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">More than a third of Israelis have shown symptoms of mental health conditions, a report found. Three years after the October 7 attack, the country's health system is still struggling to come to terms with its effects.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Israel observes October 7 anniversary with national memorial day</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5e4336cc90c0784437ce37fe1c9f4322da5c967d098180b47184b9904d6ef97b</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:15:58Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T08:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/israel-observes-october-7-anniversary-with-national-memorial-day/a-79543531--c5becbeaf308.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/israel-observes-october-7-anniversary-with-national-memorial-day/a-79543531?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Israel is holding memorial ceremonies nationwide for those killed in the October 7, 2023 Hamas terror attacks and soldiers who died in the ensuing war.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez calls snap election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:df03580cd48136e9c1ca44bc39ea9fb0aa9e7cf82b22b8822295abf1b2eb7811</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:16:01Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T07:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spanish-prime-minister-pedro-sanchez-calls-snap-election/a-79542826--8d0a8ce178ec.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spanish-prime-minister-pedro-sanchez-calls-snap-election/a-79542826?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Spanish prime minister had repeatedly insisted he would serve out his four-year term, with elections scheduled for 2027. The move comes after a major defeat for his coalition's proposed housing reforms.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Yemen launches major military operation against Houthis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:079b7f22c6f1138ad55dde1e9b787c2a77054411a7d20456dfc5b5f937f38b53</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:16:04Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T06:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/yemen-launches-major-military-operation-against-houthis/a-79542723--a2d13f53fcc7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/yemen-launches-major-military-operation-against-houthis/a-79542723?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Yemen's internationally recognized government announced a new military offensive to retake Houthi-held territory after rebels cut a key road linking the city of Taiz with Aden.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Top court hears petitions against Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e9fcf98968cc42c10b7b2ce83c917f1cac74a3452b2df2170dbfd2e9bafe33b2</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:16:07Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T05:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-top-court-hears-petitions-against-chief-election-commissioner-gyanesh-kumar/live-79542552--db693202576d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-top-court-hears-petitions-against-chief-election-commissioner-gyanesh-kumar/live-79542552?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Supreme Court heard pleas against India's beleagured poll body chief over alleged unilateral decisions related to the large-scale revision of voter lists.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Hundreds of French schools shut, teen loses hand in protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:44e16237c4199bd50cd0e284c8580f1aeb398e3197ac47bb7c54f18fbdecc5fe</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:16:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T05:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hundreds-of-french-schools-shut-teen-loses-hand-in-protests/a-79542656--d9ec9cc932b7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hundreds-of-french-schools-shut-teen-loses-hand-in-protests/a-79542656?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The student protests that rocked France last week have prompted authorities to keep up to 500 schools closed on Monday. A teenage boy lost his hand, seemingly while trying to pick up a police tear gas grenade.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Middle East oil exports recover to pre-Iran war levels despite Hormuz attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9ce3d4a66963ed6bad3bd95924746fe4ee493d95691c487386f2554f62b836c4</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:14:18Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T05:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/middle-east-oil-exports-recover-to-pre-iran-war-levels-despite-hormuz-attacks/a-79542680--cacbf5cc3f31.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/middle-east-oil-exports-recover-to-pre-iran-war-levels-despite-hormuz-attacks/a-79542680?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Gulf crude exports returned to pre-war levels in September, with producers increasingly relying on alternative routes and ship-to-ship transfers to bypass Hormuz. Iranian exports remain below the pre-war average.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US: FBI arrests woman accused of spying for China</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ed9f83c30e65248143c522eae1e173b47bef4cfd1f909adea3dcb7337ceef352</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:14:18Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T03:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-fbi-arrests-woman-accused-of-spying-for-china/a-79541849--28beb0c09d9f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-fbi-arrests-woman-accused-of-spying-for-china/a-79541849?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A California woman was arrested at Los Angeles International Airport, just before departing for China, with the US officials accusing her of spying on Taiwan's president's son.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
